    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6783c08b-cd7d-5790-b6c8-db6d4318a53d",
      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-\\frac{5}{x^{6}}+x^{2}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x^{4}}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-\\frac{5}{x^{6}}+x^{2}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x^{4}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-5x^{-6}+x^{2}+3x^{\\frac{-4}{3}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -5\\int x^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+3\\int x^{\\frac{-4}{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -5\\left(\\frac{x^{-6+1}}{(-6+1)}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{2+1}}{(2+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +3\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-4}{3}+1}}{(\\frac{-4}{3}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{1}{x^{5}}+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
