      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$\\frac{3}{x^{4}}+5\\sqrt[7]{x^{4}}+2x^{2}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(\\frac{3}{x^{4}}+5\\sqrt[7]{x^{4}}+2x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(3x^{-4}+5x^{\\frac{4}{7}}+2x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 3\\int x^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+5\\int x^{\\frac{4}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+2\\int x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 3\\left(\\frac{x^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}\\right)+5\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{4}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{4}{7}+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +2\\left(\\frac{x^{2+1}}{(2+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{1}{x^{3}}+\\frac{35\\sqrt[7]{x^{11}}}{11}+\\frac{2x^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
